{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244343-the-mandela-effect-and-reality-editing","id":1244343,"title":"The Mandela Effect and Reality Editing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-09T18:58:06-07:00","id":1244343,"title":"The Mandela Effect and Reality Editing","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I was thinking about this after reading the Seers of the Thrones book. The Mandela Effect might be a great example of Reality Editing that can be applied to a game to generate both plot hooks and atmosphere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">During the course of a campaign you can introduce elements into the game and then later suddenly change them. Be subtle about it and give no explanation for the change. I like the idea of using most of it strictly for atmosphere or to draw out paranoia in the players, also as a way of showing there are other mages out their behind the scenes doing stuff that changes reality. Most Mandela Effects have no answer that the players will be able to solve. The players might be able to pick up on some of it and investigate, a few could lead to Mysteries or plot hooks to explore. They will discover sleepers and sleepwalkers that remember the same things they do, but many more that only remember the edited reality. In any case their is no longer any hard proof in the Fallen World that those memories ever existed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Examples:</span></span><ul><li>A friend is married to a different woman and swears he has never been married to anyone else.</li> <li>You come home one day and your apartment is painted different colors.</li> <li>The name of a prominent corporation changes.</li> <li>Your mother shows you pictures of the family dog you never remember having.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">One great Meta way to use this is to explain away a change in players or characters. When introducing a new player to your group: well his character was a member of the cabal all along even if none of the other characters remember him. The same thing can be used for a player that isn't happy with his character. You let the player change characters, from that character's point of view he has been around the entire time, but from his cabal mates perspective they have never met him before.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I know some of you have probably already done this or thought of it. So what are some of your Mandela Effects?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T19:53:22-07:00","id":1244353,"title":"","content":"They do sound like archmastery shenanigans. Or God-Machine meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T20:14:33-07:00","id":1244357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244343-the-mandela-effect-and-reality-editing?p=1244353#post1244353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do sound like archmastery shenanigans. Or God-Machine meddling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't even need that. With enough reach and dice penalties several 4 and 5 dot spells could cause these effects. Reality Editing is definitly within the grasp of Adepts and Masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 08-09-2018, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T20:42:14-07:00","id":1244363,"title":"","content":"True. But mages would recognize another mages work rather easily, wouldn\u2019t they? Hence me suggesting Outside Context powers for use in Mage games. <br /> <br /> Then again, if the mages are npcs, then yeah, Mandela Effect is in full. Especially with Quiescence blurring out the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T23:05:20-07:00","id":1244392,"title":"","content":"How about a Patterning of Time ? Instead of Rewriting History, a mage can steal it. The caster would take the person's history wholesale, no temporal sympathy needed, they just take it all. The person who stole the history gets the victim's life, their resources, their family thinks its them, etc. But the mage becomes a ghost person, his original identity (and any hallows, order status, contacts, allies, resources, friends, family, etc) only comes back when the spell ends. What happened to the victim's life and the mage's stuff all depends on how Time reweaved itself afterwards.<br /> <br /> So now you can frame this as the result of an invisible war, for example, the Awakening Gambit and the Princes of Many Masks are each seizing different lives and warding certain key pawns (knowing or otherwise) as part of their moves. And the Cult of the Doomsday Clock are manipulating everything in the background, striving to use all this temporal shenanigans to transform the city into a perfect invocation site for a time devouring Gulmoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-10-2018, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T03:41:01-07:00","id":1244438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244343-the-mandela-effect-and-reality-editing?p=1244392#post1244392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Patterning of Time ? Instead of Rewriting History, a mage can steal it. The caster would take the person's history wholesale, no temporal sympathy needed, they just take it all. The person who stole the history gets the victim's life, their resources, their family thinks its them, etc. But the mage becomes a ghost person, his original identity (and any hallows, order status, contacts, allies, resources, friends, family, etc) only comes back when the spell ends. What happened to the victim's life and the mage's stuff all depends on how Time reweaved itself afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, like an Unchained Soul Pact, only not permanent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:16:25-07:00","id":1244542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244343-the-mandela-effect-and-reality-editing?p=1244438#post1244438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, like an Unchained Soul Pact, only not permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, but without bargaining (although that sounds like an interesting spell too). Pentacle mages would use it as a temporary and extreme form of cover. But certain Seers such as the Chrysalides would go the extra mile to make it indefinite, because they see another degree of separation from the Husk as a good thing. Princes of Many masks would secure places of power and even the average Seer might use it as a part of securing his Klingon Promotion.<br /> <br /> When the spell ends is the fun part. If one of the parties dies before its released, then there is nothing to be restored to normal. In that case you have the potential to either erase the dead person wholesale from history or cause a time boom (temporal equivalent of a sonic boom) that is as subtle as the ones first suggested by the OP or that could compound to Flashpoint Paradox levels, either way, it all seems to resonate with the themes of the Cult of the Doomsday Clock. The PCs could see the edges of this conflict as they go around their adventures, and the rest is Boiling Frog Theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:24:09-07:00","id":1244545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244343-the-mandela-effect-and-reality-editing?p=1244542#post1244542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, but without bargaining (although that sounds like an interesting spell too). Pentacle mages would use it as a temporary and extreme form of cover. But certain Seers such as the Chrysalides would go the extra mile to make it indefinite, because they see another degree of separation from the Husk as a good thing. Princes of Many masks would secure places of power and even the average Seer might use it as a part of securing his Klingon Promotion.<br /> <br /> When the spell ends is the fun part. If one of the parties dies before its released, then there is nothing to be restored to normal. In that case you have the potential to either erase the dead person wholesale from history or cause a time boom (temporal equivalent of a sonic boom) that is as subtle as the ones first suggested by the OP or that could compound to Flashpoint Paradox levels, either way, it all seems to resonate with the themes of the Cult of the Doomsday Clock. The PCs could see the edges of this conflict as they go around their adventures, and the rest is Boiling Frog Theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I just thought the parallel was an interesting note. And, if one doesn't mind a little crossover, they can throw in Demons as a false positive of these temporal corrections.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12488\" data-vbnamecard=\"12488\">Jeremysbrain</a> Have you read <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/956240-hack-time-is-a-series-of-tubes\">Time is a series of tubes Hack</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"da